course: dictionary
lesson: 6399
title: Murderer: a word about serious crime
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A murderer is a person who kills another person on purpose, and it is against the law. Murderer is a noun, so one person is a murderer and more than one are murderers. The clue is on purpose: a person who causes an accident is not a murderer.
explain: Read the clues in the sentences. «A murderer at the door asking where your friend is hiding» tells you the murderer wants to harm someone. Test the meaning: «Who is the murderer?» fits a mystery story if it means the person who did the killing.
explain: Some phrases add meaning. A «convicted murderer» is a murderer who has been found guilty in a court. A «mass murderer» is someone who kills many people. Both are very serious words, so use them carefully.
fact: A murderer is a person who kills another person on purpose, against the law.
fact: In law, a murderer is someone who has been convicted of murder, a very serious crime.
fact: Murder is punished with long prison sentences.
fact: «Who is the murderer?» is a question often asked in mystery stories.
fact: The German philosopher Immanuel Kant said you must not lie, even to a murderer at the door; most philosophers disagree and say protecting a person comes first.
exercise: «Who is the murderer?» What does murderer mean? | A person who works in a hospital | *A person who kills another person on purpose, against the law | A person who finds lost things | A person who tells the best jokes
exercise: What does «convicted murderer» mean? | A murderer who has just moved house | A person who is very tall | A person who has lost a game | *A murderer who has been found guilty in a court
exercise: How do you write more than one murderer? | murderes | murderer's | *murderers | murderors
test: In the puzzle, a murderer asks where your friend is hiding. What does the murderer want? | *To harm your friend | To ask for a drink | To give your friend a present | To play hide and seek
test: What makes a murderer different from someone who kills by accident? | Killing with a knife | Living in a castle | *Killing on purpose | Being very tall
exam: Which sentence uses murderer correctly? | We baked a cake and the murderer ate every slice | *The court found the man a convicted murderer and sent him to prison | The murderer of the garden was a friendly cat | The murderer sang at the school concert
